From f1ea9519a626d15dc3928ab0f18c35bb6345bae1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Maximiliano <m.lopz.montn@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 19:28:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix: surface real-time sync errors instead of dropping
 them

- syncPattern was logging every call with console.log, including a
  no-op call with no signed-in user. Drop the leftover debug logging.
- subscribeToAccountPatterns/subscribeToAccountPalettes only logged
  onSnapshot errors to the console, so a lost connection on one
  device silently stopped that device's real-time sync with no way
  for the UI to notice. Both now accept an onError callback.
- useAccount exposes a new syncStatus ('offline' | 'connecting' |
  'live' | 'error') derived from the two listeners, and recovers
  back to 'live' the next time a snapshot succeeds after an error
  (previously it would stay stuck on 'error' forever, even after the
  connection came back).
- Add test coverage for accountRepo's real-time subscriptions and
  useAccount's syncStatus state machine, neither of which had any
  tests before.
